Record the CSS transitions/animations resolve_stylist finishes (Roves).

Stylo's restyle removes finished transitions AND finished animations from the
ElementAnimationSet in the same traversal that follows Blitz's
Running -> Finished step (Stylo 0.22 matching.rs retains only entries whose
state is not Finished; a forwards fill lives on in the computed style only), so
an embedder reading BaseDocument::animations() afterwards sees them disappear
exactly like canceled ones (Element.getAnimations rejected `finished` with
AbortError, CI 43047120469, and lost forwards-filled animations, CI
43058658768). This captures every entry the state machine moves to Finished,
before the traversal, together with (keyframes animations only) an Arc of the
target's computed style at that point, i.e. the animation-* declarations that
produced it, and lets the embedder take them. animation_target_style reads the
primary or eager ::before/::after style the same way flush_pseudo_elements does,
so the embedder can compare the recorded and current declarations. Nothing in
Blitz's own behavior changes; at most FINISHED_ANIMATIONS_CAP records are kept.

Base: crates.io blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.4 + 0001. Applied in
support/blitz-v8-probe/vendor/blitz-dom; see ROVES_PATCHES.md there.

